Alternative Twilight (Remastered) - Minecraft 1.20.1 / Forge 47 backport (SkyTekx)
=================================================================================

This is a MODIFIED version of "Alternative Twilight (Remastered)" (mod id at_mod) by lvedy (Lvedy114).

  Upstream:         https://github.com/Lvedy114/alternative-twilight
                    https://modrinth.com/mod/alternative-twilight-remastered
  Upstream commit:  99f43e08adfeffe3dd689835d485a66d39d3590c (branch `old`, 2026-07-03): the Modrinth
                    0.0.2 release (3637efb, 2026-05-15) plus the Knight Phantom aurora, the expanded config
                    and the GPL-3.0 LICENSE. The newer `master` branch (8f5c978, 2026-09-09) is an
                    unfinished rewrite whose boss mechanics are empty TODO stubs, so it is not the base.
  Upstream license: GNU General Public License v3.0 (LICENSE, kept unchanged). Modrinth lists the
                    project as GPL-3.0-or-later.

This backport is distributed under the same license (GPL-3.0-or-later). Its complete source
(Corresponding Source) is public at
  https://github.com/skytekx/skytekx3-1201-server/tree/master/ports/alternative-twilight-remastered
The exact source of a given jar is that directory at the commit that added the jar to local-mods/.
Build: ports/twilightforest first (./gradlew build), then ./gradlew build in this directory; the jar
build is byte-reproducible.

Changes in this backport (version 0.0.2-1.20.1-skytekx.1, November 2026). Every source file was
modified for Minecraft 1.20.1 / Forge 47:

- Rewritten from Minecraft 1.21.1 / NeoForge 21.1 to Minecraft 1.20.1 / Forge 47, against the
  SkyTekx Twilight Forest fork (twilightforest 4.3.2508-skytekx.1, ports/twilightforest), which
  carries the TF 4.8 boss rework this mod was written for.
- Registries: DeferredHolder/DeferredItem -> RegistryObject; NeoForge ModConfigSpec -> Forge
  ForgeConfigSpec (same at_mod_config.toml keys, defaults and ranges); NeoForge events -> Forge 47
  events (LivingIncomingDamageEvent -> LivingAttackEvent, PlayerTickEvent.Post ->
  TickEvent.PlayerTickEvent END, game/mod bus subscribers).
- Spears: the 1.21 ItemAttributeModifiers and Tool components become getDefaultAttributeModifiers
  (attack damage, attack speed, Forge entity reach), getDestroySpeed and mineBlock; NeoForge's
  enum extension (enumextensions.json + EnumProxy) for the arm pose becomes HumanoidModel.ArmPose.create;
  4.8's TFToolMaterials is the fork's TwilightItemTier.
- Blood Lust: the per-level attribute curve becomes MobEffect#getAttributeModifierValue; attribute
  modifiers use fixed UUIDs derived from the upstream modifier ids.
- Mixins target the fork's classes: Naga#getMovementAI (4.8: getMovementPattern), NagaMovementPattern,
  Lich. Refmap generated by MixinGradle (SRG). The minion summoned on a shield break goes through
  ForgeEventFactory.onFinalizeSpawn, like TF's own minion goal.
- Data: 1.20.1 folder names (recipes/), recipe results use {"item": ...}; the 1.20.5+ damage type tags
  minecraft:bypasses_wolf_armor and minecraft:no_knockback do not exist in 1.20.1 and are dropped; the
  Naga venom's no-knockback rule is kept by cancelling Forge's LivingKnockBackEvent during its own hurt
  call. Item models use the forge:separate_transforms loader.
- Aurora post effect: the view matrix comes from the level PoseStack, PostChain#passes is looked up by
  its SRG name (the upstream getDeclaredField("passes") only works in a dev environment).
- Fixes to upstream behaviour:
  * the Blood Lust Curse expiry damage is applied at the start of the next entity tick instead of inside
    MobEffectEvent.Expired, which fires while the effect map is being iterated (a totem or an effect added
    on hurt would make the curse expire, and hit, again);
  * the Naga venom damage is read from the config on every hit instead of once at class load;
  * a Naga constructed before the common config is loaded keeps TF's default health instead of
    crashing on the unloaded config value;
  * the Naga venom projectile gets an entity name (entity.at_mod.naga_venom in en_us and zh_cn), which
    upstream lacks, so Jade and F3 do not show the raw key.
- Not included:
  * the eight boss music tracks (assets/at_mod/sounds/music/*.ogg, about 33 MB) and their sounds.json.
    Their metadata shows they were downloaded from Bilibili videos of unknown authorship, so the GPL
    grant of the code does not establish a right to redistribute them. The boss music system is ported
    and plays at_mod:music.<boss> (naga, lich, hydra, ur_ghast, knight_phantom, snow_queen, minoshroom,
    alpha_yeti) as soon as a resource pack defines those sound events in assets/at_mod/sounds.json;
    without one it stays silent;
  * the NeoForge in-game config screen (Forge 47 has no generic one; edit config/at_mod_config.toml);
  * the MDK template leftovers (at_mod:example_block and its block item, the "HELLO" log listeners) and
    their lang keys (item.at_mod.example_item, at_mod.configuration.items, logDirtBlock and
    magicNumber*).
